/-! # Local lifting of units along reduction

Source: blueprint `lem-sc-brauer-zero-all-curves`, Proof, Step 1.
(blueprint: lem-sc-reduction-units-epi)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme

/-- The comparison from pulled-back units to units on the reduction is an epimorphism.
Source: literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-curve-estimates/sk-prop-h2/
lem-sc-brauer-zero-all-curves.md, Proof, Step 1 and the following Claim.
(blueprint: lem-sc-reduction-units-epi)

Proof: Write i for the reduction immersion. On an affine etale V over X, base change
of i is the quotient by the pulled-back nilradical ideal. Locally over an affine open
of X, this ideal is generated by images of nilpotent elements. Each of its elements
is a finite sum of multiples of these generators and is therefore nilpotent.
Its quotient is etale over X_red and hence reduced, so the ideal is the nilradical of V.
Units lift modulo a nil ideal: lift a unit and its inverse to a and b; ab = 1 + t
with t nilpotent, and the finite geometric series in -t inverts 1 + t.
Thus the map G_m,X -> i_*G_m,X_red is locally surjective on the affine etale basis,
and is an epimorphism of sheaves. The reduction gives an equivalence of etale topoi.
Under this equivalence i^* is exact and its counit i^*i_*G_m -> G_m is an isomorphism.
The transpose of the preceding epimorphism is i^*G_m,X -> G_m,X_red, so it too is epi.
For empty or already reduced X the same reasoning applies, with zero ideal. -/
theorem epi_upperStarGmSheafToGmSheaf_reduction (X : Scheme.{u}) :
    Epi (upperStarGmSheafToGmSheaf X.nilradical.subschemeι) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme
